## Key Design Decisions

| Decision | Rationale |
|---|---|
| **Top-level `data` / `meta` / `links` envelope** | Separates payload from metadata; makes it easy to add pagination, warnings, or debug info later without breaking clients. |
| **Money as integer minor units + currency** | `8817` = $88.17. Avoids floating-point rounding errors and supports multiple currencies. |
| **ISO 8601 UTC timestamps** | Unambiguous and universally parseable. Clients localize using `timezone`. |
| **Prefixed string IDs** (`usr_`, `ord_`) | Self-describing, prevents mixing up ID types, and doesn't leak sequential database IDs. |
| **`itemsPreview` instead of full line items** | Keeps the payload light. Full details live at `links.self` for each order. |
| **Explicit `null`s** (`shipment: null`) | Clients can distinguish "no value" from "field missing" and keep a consistent schema. |
| **Enum-style `status` strings** | e.g. `pending`, `processing`, `shipped`, `delivered`, `cancelled`, `refunded`. Document the full set. |
| **`meta.totalOrderCount` + `links.allOrders`** | Tells the UI whether to show a "View all orders" link and where it points. |
| **Orders sorted by `placedAt` descending** | "Last five" is unambiguous. Document this ordering. |
| **Sensitive data excluded** | No password hashes, full payment card numbers, or internal flags. Show at most the card's last 4 digits if payment info is needed. |

