## Key Design Decisions

| Decision | Rationale |
|---|---|
| **`data` / `meta` / `links` envelope** | Separates payload from metadata and keeps the structure consistent across endpoints. |
| **Money as integer minor units** (`8997` = $89.97) | Avoids floating-point rounding errors. `currency` and `formatted` make it easy to display. |
| **ISO 8601 UTC timestamps** | Unambiguous and sortable. Clients convert to local time using `preferences.timezone`. |
| **Prefixed string IDs** (`usr_`, `ord_`) | Identify the resource type at a glance, prevent ID mix-ups, and don't expose sequential DB keys. |
| **Orders sorted by `placedAt` descending** | "Last five" means newest first. Document this contract explicitly. |
| **`recentOrders` always an array** | Return `[]` for users with no orders, never `null` or an omitted field. |
| **Explicit `null` for unknown values** (`deliveredAt`) | Clients can distinguish "not yet" from a missing field. |
| **Order summaries, not full details** | Payment info, full address history and refunds live at `links.self` to keep the payload light. |
| **`itemCount` alongside `items`** | Lets the UI show "3 items" even if you later truncate the `items` array. |
| **`stats.totalOrders`** | Tells the client whether to show a "View all orders" link. |
| **Status as lowercase enum** | Document the allowed values: `pending`, `paid`, `processing`, `shipped`, `delivered`, `cancelled`, `refunded`. |

## Security and Privacy Notes
- Never include password hashes, full payment card numbers, or internal flags.
- Only return this data to the authenticated user themselves or an authorized admin.
- Consider masking the phone and email if this endpoint might be used by roles other than the profile owner.

