## Notes

**JSON has no comment syntax.** The file above is strict, valid JSON (parseable by `JSON.parse` and most config loaders). If your generator supports JSONC / JSON5, you can annotate it directly:

```jsonc
{
  "site": {
    // Shown in <title>, the header, and the footer.
    "title": "My Static Site",

    // Absolute origin, no trailing slash.
    // Used to build absolute links for sitemaps, RSS, and canonical tags.
    "baseUrl": "https://example.com",

    // BCP 47 language tag. Falls back to "en" for any locale
    // not listed in the "locales" map below.
    "defaultLanguage": "en"
  },
  "build": {
    // Directory (relative to the project root) where HTML is written.
    // Usually gitignored.
    "outputDir": "dist",

    // Delete the contents of outputDir before each build.
    "cleanBeforeBuild": true,

    // Minify HTML/CSS/JS output.
    "minify": true
  },
  "locales": {
    "en": { "label": "English", "dir": "ltr" },
    "fr": { "label": "Français", "dir": "ltr" },
    "ar": { "label": "العربية", "dir": "rtl" }
  }
}
```

**Typical conventions for these fields**

| Field | Meaning | Common value |
|---|---|---|
| `site.title` | Site name / `<title>` prefix | `"My Static Site"` |
| `site.baseUrl` | Absolute origin for the deployed site | `"https://example.com"` |
| `build.outputDir` | Where generated files are written | `"dist"`, `"public"`, `"_site"` |
| `site.defaultLanguage` | Fallback locale for i18n | `"en"` |

**Quick usage in code**

```js
import config from "./site.config.json" with { type: "json" };

const lang = config.locales?.[config.site.defaultLanguage] ?? { dir: "ltr" };
const pageUrl = new URL(config.url.defaultPage, config.site.baseUrl).href;

console.log(`${config.site.title} -> ${config.build.outputDir} (${lang.dir})`);
console.log(pageUrl); // https://example.com/index.html
```

